<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping (Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish))",
        "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping faithfully reproduces Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py> ;
    schema:about "Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Discrete chromatophore-level cell-cell contact-dependent depolarization or 3D curved body-fin boundary mechanics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX spectral solvers for the Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear saturating PDE across stationary domain doubling scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8} (body length 2, 4, 8, 16 cm -> 3, 6, 12, 24 stripes), subcritical inhibitor-diffusion control D_I = 0.050 < d_c D_A (0 stripes), continuous growing-domain kymograph (3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes), and 2D Y-branch horizontal unzipping (3 -> 4 stripes, +0.663 domain fraction displacement)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus specimen (`pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0) extracting 115 inter-stripe spacings (3.80 mm mean wavelength at 40 mm body span, CV = 0.3435), alternating primary vs newly inserted secondary mid-trough stripe prominence ratio (2.65x), and bimodal Kondo-Asai waveform correlation (r = 0.858)",
        "reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39 short-range autocatalytic activation and long-range lateral inhibition",
        "reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 piecewise-linear saturating Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE on an expanding skin domain L(t) = L_0 exp(gamma t), mid-trough secondary stripe insertion cascade (3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 stripes) in Pomacanthus semicirculatus, and 2D horizontal Y-junction branch point unzipping in Pomacanthus imperator",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D and 2D planar piecewise-linear reaction-diffusion PDE mapped to juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus lateral flank stripes and Pomacanthus imperator Y-junction dislocations" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Pomacanthus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1995-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion.py; output: docs/media/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_comparison.png; organism: Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: e4c6766f0513e073e4470f6a811662276c20929359a8102829c89d29daf6842b; artifact_sha256: f56ad3b6f32a4c800405b224dcf0d9573c52ab752213d4ba7c15f304411e5faa; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg=5564f850c1905fb6..., datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion_reference.json=4e059d555df1a3d7..., datasets/pomacanthus_stripe_insertion/scout_manifest.json=bf877731da64b97b...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 piecewise-linear saturating Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE on an expanding skin domain L(t) = L_0 exp(gamma t), mid-trough secondary stripe insertion cascade (3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 stripes) in Pomacanthus semicirculatus, and 2D horizontal Y-junction branch point unzipping in Pomacanthus imperator | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39 short-range autocatalytic activation and long-range lateral inhibition; reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX spectral solvers for the Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear saturating PDE across stationary domain doubling scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8} (body length 2, 4, 8, 16 cm -> 3, 6, 12, 24 stripes), subcritical inhibitor-diffusion control D_I = 0.050 < d_c D_A (0 stripes), continuous growing-domain kymograph (3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes), and 2D Y-branch horizontal unzipping (3 -> 4 stripes, +0.663 domain fraction displacement) | Computer-vision segmentation of juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus specimen (`pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0) extracting 115 inter-stripe spacings (3.80 mm mean wavelength at 40 mm body span, CV = 0.3435), alternating primary vs newly inserted secondary mid-trough stripe prominence ratio (2.65x), and bimodal Kondo-Asai waveform correlation (r = 0.858); transfer_boundary: 1D and 2D planar piecewise-linear reaction-diffusion PDE mapped to juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus lateral flank stripes and Pomacanthus imperator Y-junction dislocations; does_not_claim: Discrete chromatophore-level cell-cell contact-dependent depolarization or 3D curved body-fin boundary mechanics]" ;
